---
import '../styles/prose.css';

import { site } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-11-04T21:24:40Z');
const lastUpdatedDisplay = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  hour: '2-digit',
  minute: '2-digit',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
  timeZoneName: 'short',
}).format(lastUpdated);
---

<Base
  title="Site privacy"
  description="How thebytearray.org handles your data: no cookies, no analytics, no accounts. Theme choice stays in your browser, emails only if you contact us."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Site privacy', path: '/privacy/' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-4 sm:pt-10" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="mt-6 sm:mt-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,7.5vw,3.75rem)] leading-[1.04] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance"
      >
        Site privacy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-label-lg text-on-surface-variant">
        Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated.toISOString()}>{lastUpdatedDisplay}</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose mt-10 sm:mt-12">
      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website is run by {site.company.name}, registered in {site.company.jurisdiction}, no.{' '}
          {site.company.number}, office at {site.company.office}. For any personal data this site
          handles, {site.company.name} is the data controller.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we collect on this site</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing directly. There are no cookies, no analytics scripts, no accounts and no contact-form
          server. The contact form opens your own email app, and the message never passes through
          our server.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Stored only in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          A few small preferences are saved in your own browser and never sent to us: your theme
          (light/dark), accent colour and audio playback speed in localStorage, and a short-lived
          cache of our public GitHub repository list in sessionStorage so the Open source page does
          not re-fetch on every visit. Clearing site data removes them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>If you email us</h2>
        <p>
          We receive your name, email address and message in our inbox, only to handle your request.
          Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in answering people who contact us. We do not
          share it or use it for marketing. We keep enquiry emails only as long as we need them to
          deal with your request and any related follow-up, then delete them. Our email is hosted by
          a third-party email provider acting on our instructions. Ask for deletion at any time via{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>{' '}
          and we will delete it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Hosting and delivery</h2>
        <p>
          The site is static files served by nginx behind Cloudflare, our hosting and security
          provider, which acts on our instructions and may briefly process your IP address to deliver
          and protect the site. This can involve servers outside the UK under appropriate safeguards.
          Server logs are kept briefly for security and debugging only. We run no analytics, no
          tracking pixels and no advertising on these pages.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Content loaded from other services</h2>
        <p>
          Some pages load content directly from other companies, which means your browser contacts
          them and they receive your IP address and basic request details:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>App pages with a video show its thumbnail from YouTube (Google).</li>
          <li>The Open source page lists our repositories using GitHub's public API.</li>
          <li>The About page and blog posts show profile photos from GitHub.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A video only starts loading from youtube-nocookie.com once you click play. Clicking any link
          to GitHub, Google Play or another site likewise sends your request to that service under its
          own policy. Purchases are handled entirely by Google Play; we never see your payment details.
          Per-app handling is in each app privacy policy linked in the footer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK GDPR you may ask for access to, correction or deletion of emails you sent us, and
          you may object to or ask us to restrict our handling of them. Use our{' '}
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link">contact form</a> or email us at{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you are unhappy with how we have handled your personal data, please tell us first using
          our <a href="/contact/" class="text-link">contact form</a> or by email at{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>.
          We will acknowledge your complaint within 30 days and try to put things right. You also have
          the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at{' '}
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link">
            ico.org.uk
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          4 November 2026: added the content loaded from YouTube and GitHub, the lawful basis and
          retention for emails, our processors, and your complaint and objection/restriction rights.
          These only add disclosures and rights, so they take effect immediately.
        </p>
        <p>
          If we make a material change in future, we update the date above and note it here at least
          7 days before it takes effect.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
